<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Blanshard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1894</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Blanshard was an English barrister who became the first governor of the Colony of Vancouver Island in 1849. He found that real power lay with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>, which controlled land and trade, and that there were few settlers to govern. Unpaid and frustrated, he resigned in 1851, and the Company's chief factor James Douglas succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-blanshard.jpg" alt="Richard Blanshard" width="259" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blanshard.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
